    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and favorable platoon splits. The standout play for our lineup is **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), whose matchup against Eury P\u00e9rez is elevated by a significant dynamic platoon edge and a forecasted wind blowing out, providing him an elite ceiling. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** (71.27) and **Brice Turang** (71.09) serve as core anchors; **Brice Turang** benefits from a high-efficiency matchup against a pitcher with an xERA approaching 5.00, while **Seiya Suzuki** leverages a strong park factor and a favorable platoon advantage. **Corbin Carroll** (69.45) remains an essential start despite the aggressive threat of a 1.86s pop-time catcher, as his speed profile continues to outweigh the risks inherent in his matchup against Landen Roupp.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Jose Caballero** (52.92), who was the first cut from the active roster. While **Jose Caballero** offers the high-end stolen base potential we covet, the model ultimately benched him in favor of the higher-projected efficiency of **Austin Riley** (58.35) and **Max Muncy** (58.42). The optimizer favored the latter two due to better park factors and more favorable overall matchup contexts compared to the severe difficulty of facing a sub-3.00 xERA arm like Skubal. \n\nRisk management remains a primary focus, as we are currently operating with several \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Alex Freeland**, **Max Muncy**, **Kyle Karros**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Henry Bolte**. While **Henry Bolte** (61.60) is an exciting, high-upside play at the top of the order, any unforeseen lineup shifts could depress these efficiency scores significantly. We have successfully avoided starting **Isaac Paredes**, **Cole Young**, and **Travis Bazzana** today, as their current projections did not clear the 55-point threshold required to displace our current starters. Stay vigilant regarding wind changes at the venues hosting **Kyle Karros** and **Mickey Moniak**, as those 5% boosts are baked into their strong daily efficiency ratings.",
